id: pm-vcs-annotationteardown
title: Settle annotation fixture owners before retry-bounded teardown
description: "Fix owner issue 151: Node 22 annotation teardown can encounter ENOTEMPTY in test-owned PM lock directories. Run SDK mutation refresh in supported foreground test mode, join every owned child/watcher/task, then use asynchronous recursive force removal with bounded retries. Preserve permanent cleanup failures and all attribution assertions."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[1]: "gh:unbraind/pm-vcs#151"
created_at: "2026-10-26T06:15:07.937Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-04T07:08:28.804Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-04T07:08:28.797Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-04T07:08:28.797Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: No test-owned writers survive cleanup; native transient ENOTEMPTY is retried; persistent failures remain visible; exact-head Node 22/npm/Bun gates pass.
resolution: Implemented and merged in #150 (d240868).
expected_result: The change described by this item is on main.
actual_result: "Merged in #150 as d240868; checks successful at head 4100aa1: CodeQL, codeql, test (22), test (26), windows-acceptance-launcher (22), windows-acceptance-launcher (26)."
comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-26T06:15:11.228Z",codex-agent,"The pinned SDK exposes no PmClient disposal or pending-worker drain API. Its supported foreground search refresh mode makes awaited SDK mutations finish their work before fixture teardown; annotation subprocesses are synchronous and return after child completion. Add a managed fixture for explicitly owned asynchronous child close, watcher close and pending tasks, followed by fs.promises.rm with recursive/force/maxRetries. Real native ENOTEMPTY injection must pass with retries and fail when the retry option alone is reverted; retain persistent errors. PR 150 will say Fixes #151. Ambient agent-session failures were separately reproduced and will be fixed in the next commit without weakening provenance assertions."
  "2026-10-26T06:32:39.481Z",codex-agent,"Issue 151 implementation: annotation uses a managed fixture; async afterEach waits for owned task settlement, child close (including pipes) and watcher close, then calls fs.promises.rm with recursive=true, force=true, maxRetries=8 and retryDelay=25. Early resource rejections are observed immediately and retained for teardown failure; permanent removal errors remain visible as aggregate failures. SDK mutation refresh runs in supported foreground test mode, and synchronous annotation subprocesses finish before teardown. Full annotation plus fixture regressions pass 28/28 on Node 24 and 28/28 on Node 22. Revert proofs: setting only cleanup maxRetries to zero makes the native ENOTEMPTY regression fail 0/1; restoring it passes 1/1. Removing only the resource join makes the child/watcher teardown regression fail 0/1 (child still running); restoring it passes 1/1. Commands: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"fixture cleanup retries\" test/fixture-lifetime.test.ts; node --test --test-name-pattern=\"fixture teardown joins\" test/fixture-lifetime.test.ts. Existing provenance assertions are unchanged. SDK gap: PmClient has no lifecycle disposal/pending-worker drain API, so supported foreground refresh prevents detached SDK work. Exact-head full CI and Fixes #151 PR body follow after the separate session-isolation commit."
  "2026-10-30T13:57:25.807Z",codex-agent,"Reverified issue 151 in a disposable source copy: removing only maxRetries makes the native transient-ENOTEMPTY fixture fail; restoring passes 1/1. Removing only resource settlement makes the child/watcher/task regression fail; restoring passes 1/1. Commands: node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern=\"fixture cleanup retries\" test/fixture-lifetime.test.ts; node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern=\"fixture teardown joins\" test/fixture-lifetime.test.ts. Permanent failures remain visible. Existing fixing commit aee95e4 is retained. Complete final-source release gates follow."
  "2026-10-31T17:55:10.472Z",codex-agent,"Retained aee95e4: owned tasks, child close and watcher close settle before bounded native removal, while annotation refresh stays foreground and permanent failures remain visible. The reported annotation provenance/unsafe-link scenario passes on Node 22.23.1 with the current pinned SDK. The focused Node 22 selection passes 5/5: that real annotation case, all three fixture-lifetime cases, and gate scratch ownership. Final-head full npm/Bun acceptance remains for CI under the updated orchestrator instructions; this does not close the item or issue."
  "2026-11-01T13:20:45.794Z",codex-agent,"PR 150 cubic R25 extends the original aee95e4 lifecycle fix: registered live children now receive bounded TERM/KILL escalation and teardown waits for close, including pipes, before removal. Existing task/watcher settlement, foreground SDK refresh and permanent-error reporting remain intact. The active-child regression fails when makeManagedTempDir is reverted and passes after restoration (R25). This round also puts the native path-identity fixture cleanup in finally; a real child with an intentionally retained descriptor proves invariant failure cannot strand its fixture (R34). The full fixture/integration cohort passes 201/201; fresh exact-head CI will recheck the full runtime matrix. This item and issue remain open for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-11-01T14:33:05.528Z",codex-agent,"Sixth-review extension for cubic thread PRRT_kwDOToJT7M6yWzbu: a registered live child is actively stopped with bounded TERM/KILL escalation and awaited close before fixture-root removal. The five-case fixture-lifetime suite passes under the PM-linked command; reverting the helper makes the live-child regression fail and restoration passes. The path-identity fixture now cleans in finally even on assertion failure, with a separate failing revert. Original ENOTEMPTY ownership fix and settled SDK refresh remain intact. No installer timeout was retried. Item remains in_progress for orchestrator verification."
